  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Engineer's Study, Drawn in a Workbook",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Engineer's Study, Drawn in a Workbook\"**\n\nThe site is a workbook: printed text in a calm column, and next to it things drawn by hand. What is drawn is the furniture of a study. The library is a bookcase with nightstands beside it, the tech radar is an instrument with a round scope and a knob, the race calendar is a row of paper bibs pinned by their corners. Each is drawn the way an engineer sketches: a projection that is actually constructed, a contour, a label in handwriting. A drawing here explains or holds content; none is decoration.\n\nThe page is paper in the light theme and graphite in the dark one. The text is set in a book serif. The hand reaches the frame as the owner's marginal notes: pencil rules and underlines in place of straight lines, and the labels of blocks written in handwriting. Headings and running text stay typeset.\n\n- Text is typeset, objects are drawn. A module is an object from the study before it is a widget.\n- Pencil for structure, marker for what carries meaning.\n- Handwriting (Caveat) for anything written on a drawn object.\n- Flat page. Depth comes from drawn projection, never from shadows on the page.\n- The hand is reproducible: strokes are generated from a seed and baked into paths.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Text is typeset, objects are drawn. A module is an object from the study before it is a widget.",
      "Pencil for structure, marker for what carries meaning.",
      "Handwriting (Caveat) for anything written on a drawn object.",
      "Flat page. Depth comes from drawn projection, never from shadows on the page.",
      "The hand is reproducible: strokes are generated from a seed and baked into paths."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Pencil Follows the Theme Rule",
        "body": "Pencil strokes use the page's text colour and sit on the page's ground. Marker and paper keep their own colours in light and dark.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Done Rule",
        "body": "Marker red is spent on commitment and completion, plus the mark itself. It is not an accent for links, buttons or headings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Highlighter Rule",
        "body": "Selected text and a marked passage are washed in the price sticker's yellow, as a highlighter would.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Written-On Rule",
        "body": "Caveat appears where something is written on a drawn object and where the owner labelled a block in the margin. Headings of the text and running text are never set in it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Drawn Depth Rule",
        "body": "A module shows depth by construction and hatching. A box-shadow on a card or a panel is not part of this system.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** start a new module by naming the object from the study it is, then draw that object.",
      "**Do** draw structure in pencil (the theme's text colour) and what carries meaning in marker with a darker contour.",
      "**Do** generate strokes from a seed and bake them into paths, as `bookcase.tsx` and `brand/src/gen_icon.py` do.",
